# Tools

A collection of open-source GIS and geospatial research tools developed to support interpretable, reproducible, and human-centered environmental analysis.

## Grain Checker

A lightweight QGIS plugin for testing how spatial aggregation choices affect bivariate point-density relationships.

**Keywords:** MAUP, spatial aggregation, QGIS, sensitivity analysis, spatial statistics

**Repository:** [GitHub](https://github.com/Rintozxr/Grain_Checker_QGISPlugin)

**Demo:** [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s5FHzwQrjZk)

## Parcel-Level Land-Use Continuity Tool

A QGIS-based workflow for reconstructing parcel-level land-use continuity across historical maps, designed to address boundary drift in longitudinal spatial analysis.

**Keywords:** historical GIS, land-use continuity, parcel matching, topology, transition matrices

**Demo:** [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3ipKnXsKCno)
